    code version: 0.11.0

dedup rule: a CAPTURE is (stage label, trace_id); an INSTANCE is a trace_id. An instance is
  VIOLATING iff ANY of its captures flagged (worst-verdict-wins), and IN THE DENOMINATOR iff
  ANY of its captures is VERIFIED_CLEAN or VERIFIED_FLAGGED — a capture that ERRORED is NOT
  evidence of a violation, and an instance that ERRORED in every stage was never verified.

exposure merge rule: per INSTANCE, reduce by ANY (union) — an instance is EXPOSED iff ANY of
  its captures judged >= 1 file, and its exposure is UNRECORDED iff NO capture ever recorded
  one (never merely 'found nothing' — see the three states below). Per CAPTURE, files_compared
  is SUMMED across captures with no dedup, matching total_turns(): an instance captured in two
  stages contributes both captures' counts, because both really were verified.

population size: 22 capture(s) over 15 instance(s), 392 turn(s) — controls excluded, see below
HEADLINE violation rate, per INSTANCE (a trace_id captured in several stages counts ONCE) = 1/15 = 6.7%
alongside, per CAPTURE (an instance captured in two stages counts TWICE; NOT the headline) = 2/22 = 9.1%

disagreements: none — no disagreement between any instance's captures on the violation question

